    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including both new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe endpoint is `POST /api/owners`, served through OfficeFloor function injection with DTOs generated from the OpenAPI spec.\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response, via `allOf`) both carry it. `format: date` maps to `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` entity** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field with `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")` plus getter/setter. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps it automatically by name in both directions.\n\n3. **`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`** (new function class) \u2014 one small step that sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when the body didn't supply one. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `build` and `normalize` under `govern: [ transaction ]`, matching the project's step conventions. A supplied date passes through untouched.\n\n4. **Schema/seed SQL** \u2014 added `registration_date DATE` to the owners table in all four DB dialects, and updated the hsqldb seed inserts (positional `VALUES`, used by the test profile) to include the new column so context startup succeeds.\n\nSince the PUT pipeline's `ApplyOwner` doesn't touch `registrationDate`, updates preserve the existing value.",
